<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azawagh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Azawak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Azawagh is a dry basin and a fossil river valley in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>, mainly in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> with parts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. It is grazing land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> herders and gives its name to a breed of sighthound. Its pastures were controlled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwellemmeden">Iwellemmeden</a> confederations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azawagh.jpg" alt="Azawagh" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: derivative work: T L Miles (talk) Niger_BMNG.png: Hautala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Azawagh_Niger_BMNG.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
